    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0358" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760H.68/10–345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Representative in
                        Albania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jacobs</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-17T15:00:00-05:00">October 17, 1945—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. Athens’ 1119 Oct 3 sent to Dept and repeated to Tirana for information.
                    Reference is made to Greek FonOff note regarding Greek hostages allegedly held
                    in Albanian concentration camp at Lesh. Dept would like you to report in this
                    connection any further information <pb facs="0359" n="347" xml:id="pg347"/>
                    which may have come to your attention since your last report (your despatch 87
                    Sep 7<anchor n="86" xml:id="d309-f1"/>) and any pertinent evidence which you may
                    be able to obtain by investigation or through trustworthy sources without
                    embarrassing Mission in any way.<anchor n="87" xml:id="d309-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Tirana; repeated to Athens.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d309-f1" n="86" xml:id="d309-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d309-f2" n="87" xml:id="d309-f2-content">
                <p>In his telegram 218, December 7, 1945, 4 p.m., Mr. Jacobs reported: “Deptel 100,
                    October 17, 3 p.m. Unable obtain additional information concerning Greek
                    hostages allegedly held Albanian concentration camp but will continue efforts.
                    Repeated to Athens as 7.” (760H.68/12–745)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
